# Virtual modules

IDs are `virtual:avalon/<name>`, resolved to `\0virtual:avalon/<name>` in `avalon:nitro-virtual-modules` (`nitro-integration.ts`).

| ID | Role |
|----|------|
| `renderer` | SSR entry: integrations, layouts, assets |
| `client-entry` | Hydration runtime + CSS |
| `config` / `runtime-config` | Serialized Avalon config |
| `page-routes` / `page-loader` | Discovered pages; **static** `import` (dynamic import fails in Nitro) |
| `layouts` | `wrapWithLayouts()` |
| `assets` | Client manifest `injectAssets()` |
| `island-manifest` | Preload hints |

Do not bundle build-time Vite/rolldown plugins into the Nitro server. Pre-register framework integrations with static imports — `import()` is unreliable in the Nitro bundle. Consumer `server/renderer.ts` and `entry-client.ts` should stay one-liners that re-export these virtual modules.
